Lamahatta pilot resource list, consent templates, and scripts
Because Lamahatta is teacher/institution-first and phones may be restricted in-school, build around staff devices and shared school devices.

Minimum resources (pilot-ready)

One shared laptop/desktop (if available) + login access.
One admin steward device for recovery tasks.
A stable internet point at least weekly (hotspot acceptable).
A printer is optional but helpful for offline bridging.
Staff consent / acknowledgement (template elements)
Ground this in DPDP-style consent quality (“free, specific, informed, unambiguous”) and in security safeguards expectations. 

Include:

what accounts are created and why,
what staff data is stored (name, role, official email),
acceptable use,
data handling and AI rules,
where to report issues.
Communication scripts (short)

To head/principal: “We are not introducing student AI. We are building institutional identity, teacher workflows, and governance aligned to NEP.”
To teachers: “You will save time; you won’t do more reporting. We are standardizing what you already do and making it reusable.”
To department/cluster: “Pilot is designed as a measurable proof packet (artifacts + metrics) for replication.”